#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:14 0acc195c9ab3491fa9f1423e18ffea33
msgid "What it does"
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:16 d86ebdc5f53142df8ace143afd6271e2
msgid ""
"Creates a brand-new Shopify product listing from an Airtable Model that "
"doesn't have one yet: validates the Model's data is complete enough to "
"list (descriptions, weight, a usable photo, sellable units with a valid "
"price), builds one Shopify variant per (size/range, état esthétique) "
"combination found among its sellable units, sets generic and family-"
"specific metafields, uploads product images, and pushes inventory levels "
"-- then records the new listing back into Airtable (`Annonces Shopify`) "
"so it isn't created twice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:24 c5559d7c1c6644fa9dc4cab963ca4175
msgid ""
"This is the **only script here besides `update_product`** that writes to "
"Shopify, and the only one of the two that *creates* a listing rather than"
" updating an existing one. Both are native Python in this repo -- there's"
" no external process involved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:28 5ad44ad95e8f4d4fb8c698967cd17b7f
msgid "Documentation PDF"
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:30 0a299105dc8a453ea0dda065401794b1
msgid ""
"Shared with `update_product` via `api/scripts/_product_documentation.py` "
"(upload through `api/integrations/shopify_files.py`, GraphQL)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:33 e4bc0e6dd03847b3ab211ed161f622fd
msgid ""
"**Source:** the Model's Airtable `Documentation` attachment field -- the "
"first attachment that is a PDF (MIME type, or a `.pdf` filename). Other "
"attachments are ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:35 536cb9202aac464fa1d25a15701097a7
msgid ""
"**Target:** the product metafield "
"`SHOPIFY_PDF_METAFIELD_NAMESPACE`.`SHOPIFY_PDF_METAFIELD_KEY` (default "
"`custom.pdf_descriptif`, the \"PDF Descriptif\" definition), type "
"`file_reference`, plus a companion `single_line_text_field` "
"(`custom.pdf_descriptif_airtable_id` by default) recording the Airtable "
"attachment id the Shopify file came from."
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:39 8171042fdf1f4056800561abdfead41e
msgid ""
"**Upload:** the PDF is downloaded from Airtable (signed url, fetched "
"fresh with the record) and sent through Shopify's staged upload -> "
"`fileCreate` -> poll until `READY` -> `metafieldsSet` (both metafields in"
" one atomic call)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:42 d5501171605947f688875badd07d9ed0
msgid ""
"**Change detection:** a product this script just created has no PDF yet, "
"so the upload always happens when Airtable has one (no Shopify read "
"first). Later changes are `update_product`'s job (see its own "
"\"Documentation PDF\" section)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:45 b951beb9125145188f20e0d3f73fa7a0
msgid ""
"**Size limit:** a PDF over Shopify's 20 MB limit is first compressed with"
" Ghostscript (`api/utils/pdf_compression.py`); if it's still too big, the"
" sync fails with both sizes in the message (the Airtable original is "
"never modified)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:48 b00b63a04cd44dc4a5fcd836aa98a330
msgid ""
"**Never clears:** an empty Airtable field writes nothing "
"(`documentation_status: \"absent\"`) -- there's no deletion-sync "
"convention in this project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:50 a445a15c5bcb4d97b5f823c3f9e6b900
msgid ""
"The replaced Shopify file is not deleted from the Files library (it may "
"be referenced elsewhere)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:52 96c01f5f329149768fac4cab26fce549
msgid ""
"**Scopes:** the Shopify app needs `write_files` and `read_files` "
"(confirmed missing on the RewakeDev token on 2026-09-28 -- `fileCreate` "
"answers ACCESS_DENIED without them)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:54 24a1e9808411495daacc9410431b07af
msgid ""
"**Failure handling:** attached last, after variants, so a creation rolled"
" back earlier never leaves an orphan file. It's optional content: no PDF "
"-> nothing happens. A PDF that can't be uploaded sends an alert email and"
" is reported in `details`, but the product is kept and the run is still a"
" `success`. Reconciliation then lists it under \"Documentation PDF "
"absente de Shopify\", and its bulk action retries it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:60 33de8be2914f45469e0ee33966aa945c
msgid "Idempotence (two layers)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:62 319566559d34453681ca2d7ad262c14a
msgid ""
"**Before anything else**, verify directly against Shopify (not just "
"Airtable) that no listing already exists for this Model. Airtable's own "
"record of \"does this have a Shopify id\" can be stale (a previous "
"attempt could have failed after linking but before actually creating the "
"product, or vice versa), so this always makes a real Shopify API call "
"rather than trusting Airtable alone."
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:67 f855a6ffd4c048a2a25523ea50c638ce
msgid ""
"**Immediately after** the Shopify product is created -- before "
"metafields, images, or variants -- an `Annonces Shopify` Airtable record "
"is created linking back to the Model. This is a retry-safe lock: Airtable"
" auto-maintains the reverse link, so if this run (or Cloud Tasks-style "
"retry, in the original) is re-triggered, layer 1's check finds this "
"record and stops before creating a second product. **This ordering is "
"deliberate -- don't move the lock-record creation later \"for "
"cleanliness.\"**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:74 1466b545a7434ec8b729194b4b1d0c84
msgid ""
"Neither of those two layers, on their own, stops two truly *concurrent* "
"triggers for the same Model from both passing layer 1's check before "
"either has created anything -- that's a real race, present in the "
"original Cloud Function too, not introduced by this port. It's closed by "
"a third mechanism, one level up: `api/tasks.py`'s `run_script` takes a "
"Redis lock (`RunStore.acquire_lock`) keyed by `record_id` before calling "
"this script's `run()` at all, and records an immediate `skipped` result "
"for a second concurrent trigger rather than letting it race. See "
"`docs/architecture.rst`'s `api/tasks.py` section for the full explanation"
" -- verified live: two simultaneous triggers for the same record, one "
"rejected in 5ms, the other ran normally to completion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:84 50febabf09b24a498a8a3f7e52c85f33
msgid "Safeguards added after the 2026-10-05 incident"
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:86 106cb3da1eaa473894c0313d04468d4b
msgid ""
"An Airtable automation re-triggered this script about every 40 s for one "
"Model and left duplicate products on Shopify. Three causes, three fixes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:89 8d1162cceefd464783aa68498e569253
msgid ""
"**Create and update collided.** The lock record this script writes "
"changes the Model, which fired an `update_product` on the product still "
"being created. Shopify then answered both with `409 \"This product is "
"currently being modified\"`, and the image uploads failed. Both scripts "
"now share one Redis lock per Model (`SHOPIFY_MODEL_LOCK_NAME` = "
"`\"update_product_model\"` in `api/scripts/_shopify_links.py`). Whichever"
" starts second raises `RequeueLater` and is put back on the queue until "
"the first finishes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:96 d84bed7f2d724b1f96fc07e85dd0f0df
msgid ""
"**The rollback dropped the lock while the product was still on Shopify.**"
" When the product's deletion failed (e.g. 409), "
"`_cleanup_failed_creation` deleted the Annonces Shopify record anyway, so"
" the next trigger created another copy. It now keeps the record when the "
"product isn't really gone (the next trigger then sees the product and "
"stops), and reports `cleanup_error`. A creation whose lock record can't "
"be written is rolled back right away."
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:102 cb3ac71127384b4b9a4a14df5d5bd91f
msgid ""
"**Rollbacks re-fired the automation.** A rolled-back run is recorded with"
" `rolled_back: true` (a run that crashed in a post-creation stage counts "
"too, via `failed_at_stage`). For `ROLLBACK_COOLDOWN_SECONDS` (15 min) "
"afterwards, triggers for that Model are recorded with `status: "
"\"skipped\"`, the reason and the remaining wait in `skipped_reason`. Only"
" the latest run for the Model counts. This applies to the dashboard "
"button too. Runs that failed before creating anything (plain validation "
"errors) never start a cooldown."
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:110 f2a252b70a3d48c2be59e84d5e9c1ae5
msgid "Data it touches"
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:131 9aea9eb74bee48ada19aa0756d806150
msgid "Triggering from Airtable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:133 17912729ed64469abeead8f3ec77806e
msgid ""
"An Airtable automation (\"Run script\" action, input `model_id` = the "
"Model's record id) calls the API directly with "
"`AIRTABLE_AUTOMATION_TOKEN` -- it replaces the former queue manager -> "
"Cloud Tasks -> Cloud Function chain (Celery is the queue now, with its "
"own retries and per-`record_id` lock):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:157 e56866a1226f44a8bd77b8b4f1099df5
msgid ""
"The response only confirms the run was queued; its outcome is in `GET "
"/internal/scripts/create_product_shopify/runs` (and the alert email on "
"failure). See [Authentification](./authentication.md) for the token's "
"scope."
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:161 957499327e6646e6bde55b9053f6827b
msgid "How it works"
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:163 48167ae80e004f0797ea5437184df86c
msgid ""
"`POST "
"/internal/scripts/create_product_shopify/run?record_id=recXXXXXXXXXXXXXX`"
" queues a Celery task; a missing `record_id` is rejected with `400` (same"
" query param `update_product` uses -- both take a `record_id`, they're "
"just for different tables: `update_product`'s is a Variation id, this "
"one's is a Model id)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:167 0c4be3400b0741488a9c9b049b096789
msgid ""
"Reports a `report_stage` checkpoint at each major step "
"(`checking_existing_listing`, `validating_model`, "
"`resolving_type_and_marque`, `creating_shopify_product`, "
"`creating_airtable_lock_record`, `building_metafields`, "
"`uploading_images`, `creating_variants`, `uploading_documentation`, "
"`updating_unit_listing_dates`) -- visible live via `GET "
"/internal/scripts/create_product_shopify/current` while it runs, and in "
"Grafana/Loki (`script=\"create_product_shopify\"`, `stage=\"...\"`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:173 9cbf46e75d344e0f9952161a7064a9ad
msgid ""
"Existence check, then ~15 individual field validations (each raises an "
"internal-only `_ValidationFailed`, caught once and turned into a "
"`ScriptResult` failure -- see `api/scripts/create_product_shopify.py`'s "
"module docstring for why this shape was chosen over either a bare early-"
"return chain or a full custom exception hierarchy). Among them: `Short "
"description`, `Long description`, a positive `Poids net (kg)`, `Name` and"
" `Type`, at least one `Photo neuve` (every one at least 300x300px); every"
" unit linked to the Model's Variations needs a non-empty `Prix de vente "
"HT`; every \"A vendre\" unit needs a sale price not below its `Prix de "
"rachat`, and, when it's sellable (not Abimé/Très abimé), a `Prix de vente"
" HT` above 0. A unit at 0, empty or invalid fails the run before anything"
" is created on Shopify, with a link to that unit. No sellable unit at all"
" is a failure too."
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:184 d1b30d83a0a34c39aa0cebc4fbc522fa
msgid ""
"Creates the Shopify product (shell, no variants yet), then the Airtable "
"lock record."
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:185 b7b95a34c9c24b1c89c00fcb4466c6dd
msgid ""
"Builds the metafields: a generic spec table (weight, dimensions, any non-"
"variant Specification whose name is `\"key : value\"`-shaped) plus "
"family-specific \"filter\" metafields (currently only defined for the "
"`\"Balances\"` family -- see `FAMILY_FILTER_METAFIELDS` in the source)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:189 25afc9cee96c41569f05ffe75e94f8d9
msgid ""
"Uploads product images one at a time: \"Photo neuve\" always, plus "
"marketplace photos from the *first* sellable unit that has any (see "
"\"Known risks\" below for the exact semantics here)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:192 8aab49c69c3547ce88abf463cc7bab67
msgid ""
"Groups sellable units into variant rows by `(variant value, état "
"esthétique)`, aggregating to `(min price, count)` per group; creates one "
"Shopify variant per row (the first is bundled into the product-level "
"update that also sets Shopify's `options`, matching Shopify's own "
"requirement that a product have at least one variant before more can be "
"added), and pushes each variant's inventory level. Options: \"État "
"esthétique\", plus a second option holding the Variation's "
"`Variant_value` whenever any of the Model's Variations has one "
"(`_model_has_variant_values`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:200 ea76035806614f2ab167c10107b22f55
msgid "Attaches the documentation PDF (see \"Documentation PDF\")."
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:201 89563e69fbec438dbfe84986eeb8f3ad
msgid ""
"Updates `Date de mise en ligne` on every unit that was just listed, if "
"not already set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:202 7ba6e6a723eb49b4a023dc08316b960e
msgid ""
"Sends an error-alert email (`api.services.gmail.send_alert_email`, "
"reusing the existing Google service account -- no separate SMTP "
"credential) on any failure, on a failed documentation upload, and when a "
"family filter spec is missing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:206 b2e475ba399e4eb1b28f37bb0b41f255
msgid "Deliberate deviations from the source Cloud Function"
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:208 be6f0314ef414704ba84ca755e7b3861
msgid ""
"**No pandas/numpy.** The source used pandas only for a small groupby-"
"aggregate and numpy only for incrementally building small 2D arrays; this"
" port uses a plain `collections.defaultdict` instead (see "
"`_build_variant_rows`). Behaviorally equivalent, including `sorted()` on "
"the groups to match pandas' `groupby(sort=True)` default -- this matters "
"because the *first* variant row is special-cased (bundled into the "
"options-setting product update), so group iteration order isn't cosmetic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:214 afece8c454ca400789249a1faa7e9e16
msgid ""
"**No SMTP / hardcoded credential.** The source had a Gmail app-password "
"hardcoded in plaintext. This port instead reuses the Gmail API service "
"account already configured for `api.services.gmail.create_draft` "
"(`GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS`), sending (not drafting) from "
"`ALERT_EMAIL_SENDER` to `ALERT_EMAIL_RECIPIENTS`. No new credential type,"
" and nothing plaintext."
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:219 7ad029989ec8438283a4b354b20e8629
msgid ""
"**Hardened: zero-variants-created is now a failure, not a silent "
"success.** The source logs each variant/metafield creation failure and "
"continues regardless -- if *every* variant call failed (e.g. a bad "
"payload, a Shopify API change), it still returned success with a real "
"product that has zero real variants. This port checks the count of "
"variants actually created and fails the run (with cleanup: the Shopify "
"product and Airtable lock record are both deleted) if it's zero. "
"Metafield failures are still soft/non-fatal, same as source -- only \"the"
" product is fundamentally unsellable\" is hardened."
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:227 c803cdf45ad94214937546e488aad80a
msgid ""
"**`SHOPIFY_LOCATION_ID` is now required config**, not a hardcoded "
"production value. Confirmed empirically the dev store has three "
"locations, none matching the production id the source hardcoded "
"(`84104446276`) -- see `.env.example`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:231 b4d535f224594c6a976c69136f0d14da
msgid "Known risks / things worth reviewing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:233 c437057d9feb45419f743bd42004f500
msgid ""
"This is a large, first-time port of real, previously-production business "
"logic, tested so far with unit tests (hand-written fakes) and one real "
"end-to-end run against the dev store (see below) -- not exhaustively "
"exercised against every historical edge case the source handled. Worth a "
"closer look before relying on this for real production listings:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:239 9abfa1c4ba9441928df8e96b8224f44a
msgid ""
"**Marketplace-photo semantics, preserved exactly (possibly surprising).**"
" Only the *first* unit (in Airtable's own order) with any raw `Photos "
"marketplace` entries at all contributes photos -- even if every one of "
"its photos gets filtered out by the ≥300×300px/dedup-against-\"Photo "
"neuve\" checks, the function does not keep looking at later units for one"
" that actually has a usable photo. If a Model's first-listed unit happens"
" to have only low-res marketplace photos, the listing gets **zero** "
"marketplace photos even though a later unit might have great ones. This "
"is the source's exact behavior, kept deliberately rather than \"fixed\" "
"-- confirm this is actually wanted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:247 b52ce8d4b1794ffcaeb7884fc9053e71
msgid ""
"**Metafield creation failures are silent.** Unlike the hardened variant-"
"count check above, a generic metafield that fails to create is at most "
"logged (the response status isn't even checked), never surfaces in the "
"run's result at all. A product could ship with a missing `main_table` and"
" the run would still report success. For family filter metafields, a spec"
" Airtable doesn't have (or a network error) sends an alert email listing "
"the missing ones, but the run still succeeds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:253 27fe08985d144386ab3a1fd936e93a1c
msgid ""
"~~Fixed, but worth knowing about: the second Shopify option was decided "
"by a hardcoded Type-name lookup, not by whether the Model actually needed"
" one.~~ `_resolve_option` used to return `None` (no second option at all)"
" for any Type outside two hardcoded special cases (`Micropipette`, "
"`Paillasse`/`Meuble sous paillasse`) -- confirmed live: a genuinely "
"multi-variant Model (two distinct sizes) whose Type was neither of those "
"got created with **only one Shopify option**. Now detected from whether "
"*any* of the Model's Variations has a non-empty `Variant_value`, with or "
"without stock (`_model_has_variant_values`); the Type name still only "
"picks a nicer option label for the two known families, falling back to a "
"generic `\"Variante\"` otherwise. A product created before this fix with "
"only one option is repaired by its next `update_product` run, which "
"decides the options from Airtable and recreates the variants under them "
"(see `docs/update_product.md`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:265 34b2ba260e364dbc92253217f33f8050
msgid ""
"**`SHOPIFY_API_VERSION` is `2025-01`** (this project's existing shared "
"default), **not** `2025-07` (what the source was actually written and "
"validated against). No equivalence check has been done between these two "
"versions for the specific mutating endpoints this script uses "
"(product/variant/metafield/image/inventory writes) -- worth a deliberate "
"check, not an assumption, before trusting this in production."
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:270 e2ebf213adeb4d809c5458428fb1d21b
msgid ""
"**Family-specific filter metafields only cover `\"Balances\"`** (ported "
"as-is from the source's own `METAFIELDS` dict) -- every other family gets"
" only the generic spec table, no dedicated filter metafields. If other "
"families need filters, that mapping needs extending; nothing in this port"
" adds new families beyond what the source had."
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:274 895fa43647b941359d4ae92ba5471264
msgid ""
"**The three-repo naming quirk in `Model.fields[\"Status (from Annonces "
"Shopify (dev))\"]` is real, not a typo** -- copied byte-for-byte from the"
" source. It's a rollup field whose own name happens to contain "
"`\"(dev)\"` even when read against the production base. If this field is "
"ever renamed in Airtable, this string must be updated to match exactly, "
"or the \"already has an active listing\" short-circuit silently stops "
"working (falls through to always re-checking Shopify directly, which is "
"safe but slower -- not a silent-corruption risk, just worth knowing this "
"specific string is load-bearing)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:281 b62df0514f3042dfac494047e2ee109b
msgid ""
"~~No dedicated unit test for the \"network error on the initial product-"
"creation POST\" path~~ -- covered by `tests/test_shopify_rest.py`, added "
"alongside the 409 fix below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../create_product_shopify.md:283 4bb84bdee7634a8da109e0112e7b3f8e
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Concurrent image uploads to the same product can 409 -- now uploaded "
"one at a time** (`IMAGE_UPLOAD_WORKERS = 1` since 2026-10-05: the retries"
" below still let 1 image in 7 fail in production, which rolled the whole "
"creation back). They used to upload in parallel to *one* product; "
"Shopify's Admin API rejects a same-product write that collides with "
"another one in flight with `409 {\"errors\": {\"product\": [\"This "
"product is currently being modified. Please try again later.\"]}}` -- "
"confirmed live against the dev store (7 concurrent image uploads via "
"`ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=3)` reliably produced at least one 409). "
"Unlike a network error or 5xx, this isn't ambiguous about whether the "
"write applied -- Shopify says outright it didn't -- so "
"`ShopifyAdmin._request` now retries a 409 with backoff regardless of HTTP"
" method. See `tests/test_shopify_rest.py` for the retry-matrix coverage."
msgstr ""

